{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"cd0349dceb6cd1e7","name":"card_event_island_fighting","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Japan/BrothersInArms/events/card_event_island_fighting","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"ISLAND DEFENSE","text":"Draw a card if your HQ has 10 or less defense. Give your HQ +8 defense.","flavorText":"During WWII, the Japanese employed various strategies to defend the islands in the Pacific. Their defensive tactics involved fortified positions, underground tunnels, guerrilla warfare, naval power, and kamikaze attacks. They constructed extensive fortifications, including bunkers and tunnels, to protect their troops and supplies. Guerrilla tactics such as hit-and-run attacks and ambushes were used in areas where direct defense was not possible. The Japanese Navy played a crucial role in coastal defense, using naval guns and vessels to repel enemy assaults. Kamikaze suicide attacks were also employed as a desperate measure. However, despite their efforts, the overwhelming resources of the Allied forces eventually led to the recapture of the Pacific islands from Japanese control.","faction":"Japan","type":"order","rarity":"Common","cost":4,"operationCost":0,"attack":0,"defense":0},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_event_island_fighting","title":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_event_island_fighting_title","SourceString":"ISLAND DEFENSE","LocalizedString":"ISLAND DEFENSE"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::order","faction":"EFactionEnum::Japan","kredits":4,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_event_island_fighting_text","SourceString":"Draw a card if your HQ has 10 or less defense. Give your HQ +8 defense.","LocalizedString":"Draw a card if your HQ has 10 or less defense. Give your HQ +8 defense."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_event_island_fighting_history","SourceString":"During WWII, the Japanese employed various strategies to defend the islands in the Pacific. Their defensive tactics involved fortified positions, underground tunnels, guerrilla warfare, naval power, and kamikaze attacks. They constructed extensive fortifications, including bunkers and tunnels, to protect their troops and supplies. Guerrilla tactics such as hit-and-run attacks and ambushes were used in areas where direct defense was not possible. The Japanese Navy played a crucial role in coastal defense, using naval guns and vessels to repel enemy assaults. Kamikaze suicide attacks were also employed as a desperate measure. However, despite their efforts, the overwhelming resources of the Allied forces eventually led to the recapture of the Pacific islands from Japanese control.","LocalizedString":"During WWII, the Japanese employed various strategies to defend the islands in the Pacific. Their defensive tactics involved fortified positions, underground tunnels, guerrilla warfare, naval power, and kamikaze attacks. They constructed extensive fortifications, including bunkers and tunnels, to protect their troops and supplies. Guerrilla tactics such as hit-and-run attacks and ambushes were used in areas where direct defense was not possible. The Japanese Navy played a crucial role in coastal defense, using naval guns and vessels to repel enemy assaults. Kamikaze suicide attacks were also employed as a desperate measure. However, despite their efforts, the overwhelming resources of the Allied forces eventually led to the recapture of the Pacific islands from Japanese control."},"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Common","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::BrothersInArms","isInPermanentPool":true,"soundEnterPlay":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'War_UI_Drum_Movement_Taiko_Hits_1'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/War_UI/Waves/Drum_Movements/War_UI_Drum_Movement_Taiko_Hits_1.0"},"Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/Japan/Spring2023Candidates/t_island_defense.t_island_defense","SubPathString":""},"artist":"Look and Learn","historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/HistoricalPhotos/ISLAND_DEFENS